([P1] Orvan Grain Port is holding vessels outside the harbour as a dock strike) Tj
T*
(that began on 14 September continues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Two grain berths are closed. The port is loading at reduced speed on the) Tj
T*
(berths that remain open.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] Several bulk carriers are waiting in the roads, according to port agents.) Tj
T*
(Some have been diverted to other loaders.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Hammer Freight, a bulk operator, says it has moved ships to Vanir for wheat) Tj
T*
(cargoes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The port authority says it cannot estimate when normal working will resume.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The queue outside the harbour is being managed by the port authority, which) Tj
T*
(is giving priority to vessels that were already on the berth list when the) Tj
T*
(strike began. Agents say some owners have chosen to wait rather than divert,) Tj
T*
(because a later cargo may still earn a better price than a substitute load) Tj
T*
(elsewhere. Others have given up on the port for this month and are looking for) Tj
T*
